      "message": "Gemini review:\n\n**1. Unhandled Return Value in Status Register Read**\nIn the newly added `cros_flash_npcx_wait_ready_and_wd` function, the return value of `cros_flash_npcx_get_status_reg` is ignored:\n\n```c\n// Current code:\ncros_flash_npcx_get_status_reg(dev, SPI_NOR_CMD_RDSR, \u0026reg);\nif ((reg \u0026 SPI_NOR_WIP_BIT) \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 (reg \u0026 SPI_NOR_WEL_BIT) \u003d\u003d 0)\n    break;\n```\n\nIf the underlying SPI transaction fails, `reg` will remain uninitialized or contain stale memory, leading to unpredictable behavior or a false positive evaluation. \n\n*   **Remediation:** Check the return value and handle errors appropriately. Note that this same bug appears to exist in the pre-existing `cros_flash_npcx_wait_ready_and_we` function. I highly recommend fixing it in both places.\n\n```c\n// Suggested fix:\nint ret \u003d cros_flash_npcx_get_status_reg(dev, SPI_NOR_CMD_RDSR, \u0026reg);\nif (ret !\u003d 0) {\n    return ret; // Propagate the error upward\n}\nif ((reg \u0026 SPI_NOR_WIP_BIT) \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 (reg \u0026 SPI_NOR_WEL_BIT) \u003d\u003d 0) {\n    break;\n}\n```",
